#: kstart.C:143
msgid "Command to execute."
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:144
msgid ""
"A regular expression matching the window title.\n"
"If you do not specify one, then the very first window\n"
"to appear will be taken. Not recommended!"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:147
msgid "Desktop where to make the window appear. "
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:148
msgid "Make the window appear on all desktops"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:149
msgid "Iconify the window"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:150
msgid "Maximize the window"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:151
msgid ""
"The window type: Normal, Desktop, Dock, Tool, \n"
"Menu, Dialog or Override"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:152
msgid ""
"Jump to the window even if it is started on a \n"
"different virtual desktop"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:154
msgid "Make the window always stay on top of any other window"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:155
msgid "The window does not get an entry in the taskbar"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:162
msgid "KStart"
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:163
msgid ""
"Utility to launch applications with special window properties \n"
"such as iconified, maximized, a certain virtual desktop, a special "
"decoration\n"
"and so on."
msgstr ""

#: kstart.C:180
msgid "No command specified"
msgstr ""

#, fuzzy
#~ msgid ""
#~ "\n"
#~ " Copyright (C) 1997, 1998 Matthias Ettrich (ettrich@kde.org)\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ " Utility to launch legay applications with special KDE window properties\n"
#~ " such as iconified, maximized, a certain virtual desktop, a special "
#~ "decoration\n"
#~ " or sticky. Furthermore you can exclude the window from getting the focus "
#~ "or\n"
#~ " force the window manager to keep the window always on top.\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " In addition, the -activate switch will jump to the window even if it is\n"
#~ " started on a different virtual desktop\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Usage:\n"
#~ " %1 <command> [-window <regular expression>] [-desktop <number>]\n"
#~ "              [-sticky] [-iconify] [-maximize] \n"
#~ "              [-decoration tiny|none] [-activate] [-nofocus] [-staysontop]\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " If you do not specify a regular expression for the windows title,\n"
#~ " then the very first window to appear will be taken. Not recommended!\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Example usage:\n"
#~ " %2 \"xclock -geometry 80x80-0+0\" -window xclock \\\n"
#~ "        -decoration tiny -sticky -nofocus -staysontop\n"
#~ " puts a tiny decorated, sticky xclock on the top right corner of the "
#~ "screen,\n"
#~ " that does not even get focus (and therefore has no entry in the taskbar).\n"
#~ " Note that you can still close it with the right mouse button.\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " "
#~ msgstr ""
#~ "\n"
#~ " Copyright (C) 1997, 1998 Matthias Ettrich (ettrich@kde.org)\n"
#~ "\n"
#~ " On ptit osti po-z enonder des vîs programes ki leu purnea KDE sont-st on "
#~ "pô\n"
#~ " speciåles, par egzimpe metuwes a imådjete, å pus grand, avou des "
#~ "gåliotaedjes  ene miete drole,\n"
#~ " ou cwand ele sont-st aclapeyes. Si vos voloz, ces purneas la ni seront måy "
#~ "'ovrantes' oudôbén\n"
#~ " vos poloz foirci li manaedjeu di purneas a lzès leyî tofer so li dzeu.\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Å dzeu do martchî, li tchûze -activate potchrè sol purnea minme si\n"
#~ " elle e-st enondeye dins èn ôte forveyu scribanne\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Po s' è siervi:\n"
#~ " %s <command> [-window <regular expression>] [-desktop <number>]\n"
#~ "              [-sticky] [-iconify] [-maximize] \n"
#~ "              [-decoration tiny|none] [-activate] [-nofocus] [-staysontop]\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Si vos n' metoz nole 'regular expression' pol tite do purnea,\n"
#~ " c' est li prumî purnea ki serè prindu. Ci n' est waire ene boune ideye!\n"
#~ " \n"
#~ " Par egzimpe:\n"
#~ " %s \"xclock -geometry 80x80-0+0\" -window xclock \\\n"
#~ "        -decoration tiny -sticky -nofocus -staysontop\n"
#~ " aclaprè on ptit gålioté 'xclock' al copete a droete delwaitroûle;\n"
#~ " ci purnea la ni serè måy dispierté (èt do côp, i n' est nén rprindu è bår "
#~ "ås bouyes).\n"
#~ " Mågré tot, vos l' såroz co cloyu avou li droet boton del soris.\n"
#~ " \n"
